optimizer.step()
epoch_loss += loss.item()
print(f"Epoch {epoch}: loss={epoch_loss:.4f}")
After training, evaluate on a validation/test set:
model.eval()
with torch.no_grad():
preds = model(X_val) # shape (N_val,)
predicted_labels = (preds > 0.5).int()
accuracy = (predicted_labels == y_val).float().mean()
print("Validation accuracy:", accuracy.item())
Use metrics like accuracy, precision/recall, or AUC. For binary options, you may also simulate the predicted
trade outcomes on historical data to compute expected return.
